+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `features/todomvc.feature` and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Build handoff (Shipwright / Crew)
+
+- **Stack:** Vanilla JavaScript. No preprocessors (no Sass/CoffeeScript/TS build). ES modules or a single `js/app.js` are both acceptable; keep components split where it reads well (`js/models/todo.js`, `js/controllers/todos.js`).
+- **Markup:** Start from `assets/app-template.index.html`. Remove the HTML comments when done. Keep `node_modules/todomvc-common/base.css` untouched; put any overrides in `css/app.css` (minimal). Double-quotes in HTML, single-quotes in JS/CSS (per spec).
+- **Persistence:** Vanilla `localStorage`, key `todos-vanilla`. Each item uses keys `id`, `title`, `completed`. Do NOT persist editing state.
+- **Routing:** Hash routing `#/` (all), `#/active`, `#/completed` (also allow `#!/`). Use a `hashchange` listener (no need for Director in vanilla). Active filter persists across reload naturally via `location.hash`; confirm the scenario `Active filter persists across reload` still holds.
+- **Constants:** use `var ENTER_KEY = 13;` (and an ESC_KEY constant) rather than raw keyCodes.
+- **Dependencies:** README/package already name `todomvc-common` + `todomvc-app-css`; ensure `node_modules` vendoring keeps only files the app loads (see `.gitignore` convention). Test runner is Cucumber + happy-dom (step defs under `features/support/`).
+
+## Coverage gaps closed this pass
+
+Added three scenarios the spec required but the prior draft omitted: editing input focus on activation, edit-save on blur (besides Enter), and the `<strong>`-wrapped counter number.
+
+## Open
+
+- None blocking. Awaiting QM on the watchbill, then Shipwright for the build.
