+Feature: TodoMVC
+  As a task-bearing user
+  I want a browser todo list that adds, completes, edits, filters, and remembers my items
+  So that I can track work without losing it between sessions
+
+  Rule: Adding and removing todos
+
+  Scenario: Empty list hides the main and footer sections
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: New todo input is focused on page load
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    Then the new todo input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Entering a title creates and appends a todo
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    When I enter "Buy milk" in the new todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "Buy milk" is present
+
+  Scenario: New todo title is trimmed before storing
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    When I enter "  Walk the dog  " in the new todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "Walk the dog" is present
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only new todo is ignored
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    When I enter "   " in the new todo input and press Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Each todo item exposes a destroy button
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | Tidy  | false     |
+    Then the todo "Tidy" has a destroy button
+
+  Rule: Completing todos
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo marks it completed
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title      | completed |
+      | Write code | false     |
+    When I toggle the todo "Write code"
+    Then the todo "Write code" is marked completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all completes every todo
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | false     |
+      | B     | false     |
+    When I toggle the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then the todo "A" is marked completed
+    And the todo "B" is marked completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects all todos completed individually
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | false     |
+      | B     | false     |
+    When I toggle the todo "A"
+    And I toggle the todo "B"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking one todo unchecks toggle-all
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+      | B     | true      |
+    When I toggle the todo "A"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Rule: Editing todos
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a label enters editing mode
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title      | completed |
+      | Read book  | false     |
+    When I double-click the label of "Read book"
+    Then the todo "Read book" is in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves the trimmed title on Enter
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title     | completed |
+      | Old title | false     |
+    When I edit the todo "Old title" to "  New title  " and press Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "New title" is present
+    And the todo "New title" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Editing to empty destroys the todo
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title   | completed |
+      | Doomed  | false     |
+    When I edit the todo "Doomed" to "" and press Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Escape during edit discards the change
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Keep me  | false     |
+    When I edit the todo "Keep me" to "Changed" and press Escape
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "Keep me" is present
+    And the todo "Keep me" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Editing input receives focus when entering edit mode
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Focus me | false     |
+    When I double-click the label of "Focus me"
+    Then the edit input of "Focus me" is focused
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves the trimmed title on blur
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title     | completed |
+      | Old title | false     |
+    When I edit the todo "Old title" to "  Blur title  " and blur the input
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "Blur title" is present
+    And the todo "Blur title" is not in editing mode
+
+  Rule: Counting and clearing
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows singular "item" for one active todo
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | Only  | false     |
+    Then the counter reads "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows plural "items" for multiple active todos
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | false     |
+      | B     | false     |
+    Then the counter reads "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter excludes completed todos from the active count
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+      | B     | false     |
+    Then the counter reads "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter number is rendered inside a strong element
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | false     |
+      | B     | false     |
+    Then the counter number is wrapped in a strong element
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes completed todos
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+      | B     | false     |
+    When I click the clear completed button
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "B" is present
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed is hidden when nothing is completed
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | false     |
+      | B     | false     |
+    Then the clear completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed unchecks toggle-all
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+      | B     | true      |
+    When I click the clear completed button
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Rule: Persistence
+
+  Scenario: Todos and their completed state survive a page reload
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Persist me  | false     |
+    When I complete the todo "Persist me"
+    And I reload the app
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "Persist me" is present
+    And the todo "Persist me" is marked completed
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist under the todos-vanilla localStorage key
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Store me | false     |
+    Then the localStorage key "todos-vanilla" holds a JSON array of objects
+    And every object in that array has the string keys "id", "title", and "completed"
+
+  Rule: Routing and filtering
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only incomplete todos
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+      | B     | false     |
+    When I open the "Active" filter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "B" is present
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+      | B     | false     |
+    When I open the "Completed" filter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "A" is present
+
+  Scenario: All filter shows every todo
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+      | B     | false     |
+    When I open the "All" filter
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+
+  Scenario: Selected filter link reflects the active route
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | false     |
+      | B     | false     |
+    When I open the "Active" filter
+    Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across reload
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+      | B     | false     |
+    When I open the "Completed" filter
+    And I reload the app
+    Then the "Completed" filter link is selected
+    And the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "A" is present
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo in the active filter hides it
+    Given the app loads with the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | false     |
+      | B     | false     |
+    When I open the "Active" filter
+    And I complete the todo "A"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item titled "B" is present
